the 10 miners have been trapped  underground for almost two weeks they  were digging for coal in cohuila in  mexico when a tunnel wall collapsed and  the shaft was flooded  rescue workers have been pumping water  out of the mine families are frustrated  at how long it's taken  they must work day and night they  shouldn't stop but they do because the  pumps get blocked if the men are alive  they must be desperate it's too much  that is why we're speaking out because  we want help  more than 300 soldiers and other  emergency services personnel including  six military scuba divers have joined  the effort  rescue workers are hopeful water levels  may soon be low enough to enter at least  one of the flooded shafts  the rescuers have assessed the  conditions underground they have gone  down a significant part of the shaft but  they have not reached the bottom yet  mexico's main coal producing region has  seen a series of fatal mining accidents  over the years  the worst was in pastor de conscious in  2006 killing 65 people only two of the  bodies were retrieved  i won't live here until my brother is  found i don't want the same thing to  happen as in pasta the controls my  cousin was trapped there and they never  got him out so many accidents like this  happen in the mines and the government  does nothing  here in gohuila five miners were able to  escape but no contact's been made with  the men left behind  all their families can do now is hope  they're found alive  victoria gatenbee al jazeera
 

